course: dictionary
lesson: 1239
title: Words for rough and bumpy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Bumpiness is a noun, a name for a thing. It tells you how bumpy something is. A road full of lumps and holes has a lot of bumpiness, and a smooth floor has very little. Look for the word bump inside it, and you will be close to the meaning.
explain: The word is also used for a feeling. «A little bit of bumpiness» on a plane means the aircraft is being shaken up and down for a while. Pilots speak calmly so that nobody panics, and it is safe if you stay belted in. The words around a word show you which meaning is being used.
explain: In science, bumpiness helps you test friction. A toy car rolls a long way on a smooth floor, but it slows down on carpet or sand, because those surfaces have more bumpiness. Rougher surface, more friction.
fact: Bumpiness means how bumpy something is.
fact: Bumpiness can also mean the feeling of being shaken up and down, like on a rough road or a bumpy flight.
fact: «The bumpiness of the road» means how rough the road is.
fact: «A bit of bumpiness» means a little shaking, for example on a plane.
fact: More bumpiness usually means more friction, so a toy car slows down sooner.
exercise: Pilots say «a little bit of bumpiness» is coming. What does it mean? | *Shaking up and down during the flight | Free drinks for every passenger | The plane is about to land in the sea
exercise: In a science test, which surface would have the most bumpiness? | A carpet with thick loops | *A stony path full of lumps and holes | A smooth, polished floor
exercise: Which word names how rough or bumpy a surface is? | smoothness | *bumpiness | stillness
test: In a toy car test, the car rolls furthest on which surface? | *A smooth floor | Carpet | Grass | Sand
test: Mia says the bus ride was all bumpiness. What does she mean? | The bus was painted with spots | *The bus shook her up and down all the way | She was bored and sleepy | She enjoyed a quiet, smooth ride
exam: Which sentence uses bumpiness to mean how rough a surface is? | The sky was grey and wet | *The bumpiness of the road made the cups rattle | He ran very fast | She was happy about her new bike
